WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.040
Hi, I'm Georgie from BBC Learning English and

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.800
maybe you've heard of conditionals -

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.440
the zero, the first, the second, the third.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.080
But did you know that you can mix them up to have new meanings?

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.680
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.000
Now, we could say that our lives now are a result

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.880
of a chain of events that happened in the past.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.840
I live in London now because I applied for a job in the past.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.120
Neil has another example of this.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.680
I am so tired.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.320
I hardly slept last night.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.640
If I'd slept properly, I wouldn't be so tired now.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.920
So, Neil is tired now. Why?

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.640
Because he didn't sleep well in the past.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.320
Now, this is a type of mixed conditional.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.160
You might recognise the third
conditional structure in the first part

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.200
and the second conditional structure
in the second part,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.120
but we'll come back to the structure later.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.000
For now, you just need to know that
this type of mixed conditional is

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.480
for expressing how your life now is
affected by something that happened

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.560
in the past.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.080
Let's hear more examples.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.880
If I hadn't got this job, I would probably still be in Korea.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.360
George used to live in South Korea.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.760
Does he live there now?

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.200
No, he lives in London, working for the BBC.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.000
Again, he's imagining how a past event
influenced his present reality.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.920
He got the job in the past,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.920
so now he lives in London, not Korea.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.160
Let's hear from Pippa.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.520
So if Covid hadn't happened, I wouldn't

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.040
live where I live now because I wouldn't be able to work from home

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.640
and I wouldn't be able to live outside of London.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.280
Since the pandemic, a lot more people are able to work from home.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.240
Now Pippa's job is in London,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.120
but because of the pandemic, she's able to live outside of London

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.640
because she doesn't have to come into the office every day.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.880
Something in the past is affecting her life now.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.600
What about Buli and Phil?

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.240
If I hadn't learnt Spanish when I was younger,

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.600
my life would be very different now.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.240
If I hadn't got married, I wouldn't be working in London right now.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.000
OK, now you know when to use it.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.680
But how do you use it?

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.920
Pause the video and think about which
structures are used to make this type

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.840
of mixed conditional.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.080
The structure is the past perfect in the 'if' clause and 'would'

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:19.560
plus a base verb in the main or result clause. To recap,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:24.800
this mixed conditional is about how
past events are affecting your life now.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.800
If I had eaten breakfast, I wouldn't be so hungry now.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.920
Time for lunch.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.880
If you need more help with conditionals,

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.720
check out the rest of the Conditionals with Georgie series

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.960
and download a free worksheet on our website. See you next time!

